  "definition": "Multilayer insulation (MLI) limits radiative heat exchange between spacecraft hardware and its surroundings. A blanket stacks thin, low-emittance reflective foils with low-conductance spacer material. The reflective surfaces reduce layer-to-layer radiation; spacers keep adjacent foils apart and restrict solid conduction.[^1][^3]",
